	'pg_people_t' => 'People at the Slab',
	'pg_people_lede' => 'Six dedicated craftspeople run Himuro Gelato at 14 Quay Lane. From morning fruit preparation to the final evening scoop, our small team shares an obsession with temperature and balance.',
	'pg_people_h1' => 'The kitchen team: Ines, Tomas, and Amara',
	'pg_people_p1' => 'Ines Varga founded Himuro Gelato in 2019 and remains our principal maker at the cold slab, levelling tins and ensuring every churn meets our standard. Tomas Lind manages the morning batch freezer, weighing ingredients at dawn and executing eleven-minute churn cycles with mechanical precision. Amara Okafor leads flavour development and fruit buying, sourcing local orchard pears, plums, and figs, and working directly with regional growers to capture natural acidity and sweetness without artificial extracts.',
	'pg_people_h2' => 'The counter team: Mei, Rafael, and Sofie',
	'pg_people_p2' => 'Mei Han leads the front counter, greeting guests across the glass, explaining flavour profiles, and curating daily service with quiet grace. Rafael Moreno manages the evening service and the −18 °C hold shelf, carefully tagging set-aside tubs and ensuring takeaway orders are packaged securely for the walk home. Sofie Brandt bakes our crisp wafer biscuits and hand-rolls cones each morning on warm irons, filling the shop with the comforting scent of toasted butter and vanilla.',
	'pg_people_h3' => 'Customer story: The night-shift nurse',
	'pg_people_p3' => 'Just before our lights dim at 20:40, a local hospital nurse arrives at 14 Quay Lane on her way to night shift. She always orders a double cup for €5.60, typically pairing Black Sesame Milk with Dark Cocoa Sorbet. Sitting on our exterior bench for five quiet minutes, she savours the dense, cold creaminess before walking down the dock. It is a calm, necessary threshold between daytime rest and an arduous evening under hospital lights.',
	'pg_people_h4' => 'Customer story: Sunday family collections',
	'pg_people_p4' => 'Every Sunday afternoon, a father arrives to collect a pre-reserved 1 L family tub for €21.00, accompanied by a reusable insulated carry bag. Having submitted his reservation before the 15:00 deadline, his tub is packed with Hazelnut Gianduja and Lemon Ricotta and held at −18 °C. Collecting it by name from Rafael Moreno, he carries it home to Larkhaven’s residential streets for a post-dinner family ritual that has continued unbroken since 2019.',
	'pg_people_h5' => 'Customer story: The walk over the bridge',
	'pg_people_p5' => 'On Friday evenings, a university student walks into the shop to collect a 500 ml walk-home tub of Burnt Fig & Plum for €12.00. Tucking the cold paper container into her satchel, she begins her journey across the harbour bridge toward home. Even in early autumn, the dense churn holds its structure across the water, arriving at her kitchen table perfectly tempered, soft enough to spoon immediately without any ice forming around the rim.',
