	'pg_people_more' => 'Visit the counter and say hello →',
	'pg_visit_t' => 'Visit Quay Lane',
	'pg_visit_lede' => 'Join us at 14 Quay Lane in Larkhaven’s Harbour Quarter for freshly churned gelato. We offer fourteen seats inside our calm cold-store space and six seats outside along the quay.',
	'pg_visit_h1' => 'Location and opening hours',
	'pg_visit_p1' => 'Himuro Gelato is located at 14 Quay Lane, Harbour Quarter, Larkhaven. We are open Wednesday through Sunday from 12:00 to 21:00. On Mondays and Tuesdays, our shop is closed for deep cleaning, maintenance, and ingredient preparation. If you wish to reserve a takeaway tub from our morning churns, please submit your reservation by 15:00 on the day of collection. You can contact us by phone at +00 10 4820 1907 or email hello@himurogelato.example.',
	'pg_visit_h2' => 'How to reach the Harbour Quarter',
	'pg_visit_p2' => 'Reaching our workshop on Quay Lane is straightforward on foot, by bicycle, or via local public transit. From the Larkhaven central railway station, take the local bus down to the Harbour Quarter terminal, which leaves you just a three-minute stroll from our front glass. Cyclists will find sturdy bike racks directly opposite our front entrance. If arriving by car, short-stay harbour parking bays are available along Quay Lane, though we encourage walking down the waterfront whenever possible.',
	'pg_visit_h3' => 'Seating, atmosphere, and accessibility',
	'pg_visit_p3' => 'Our restored cold-store offers fourteen seats inside around low wooden counters and six exterior seats on stone benches overlooking the harbour. The interior maintains a calm, quiet atmosphere with natural daylight, brushed steel counters, and soft acoustics. Our entrance is step-free with a wide threshold suitable for wheelchairs and pushchairs, and our seating layout accommodates mobility devices comfortably. Service dogs are welcome, and our counter staff are always glad to assist with door access.',
	'pg_visit_h4' => 'Can I bring gelato to take away on transit?',
	'pg_visit_p4' => 'Yes, our 500 ml walk-home tubs (€12.00) and 1 L family tubs (€21.00) are designed specifically for travel. When packed in our reusable insulated carry bag (€3.00), gelato remains frozen and stable during your journey, allowing ample time to travel across Larkhaven by bus, train, or foot. For best results, place the tub into your home freezer immediately upon arrival, or let it temper for five minutes if enjoying right away.',
	'pg_visit_label' => 'Find the counter',
	'pg_newsletter_t' => 'The Flavour Note',
	'pg_newsletter_lede' => 'Subscribe to The Flavour Note, our weekly email sent every Tuesday morning. Receive the upcoming week\'s churn schedule, rotating specials, and kitchen notes directly in your inbox.',
	'pg_newsletter_h1' => 'What arrives in The Flavour Note every Tuesday',
	'pg_newsletter_p1' => 'Every Tuesday morning, before our Wednesday opening, we send The Flavour Note to subscribers. Written by Amara Okafor and Ines Varga, this short email lists the six standing flavours alongside any rotating batches scheduled for the coming week. You will learn which seasonal fruits arrived at Quay Lane, when specialty tubs will be available for set-aside, and any schedule updates before our batch freezers spin on Wednesday morning.',
	'pg_newsletter_h2' => 'How we respect your inbox and privacy',
	'pg_newsletter_p2' => 'We send exactly one email each week on Tuesday. We never share subscriber addresses, include third-party advertising, or send promotional spam. Subscribing is simple: enter your email address in the field below and confirm the request. If you ever wish to unsubscribe, a single click at the bottom of any email removes you immediately. You can also reach our team directly at hello@himurogelato.example with any questions regarding our weekly notes.',
	'pg_newsletter_label' => 'Subscribe',
	'pg_contact_t' => 'Contact the Workshop',
	'pg_contact_lede' => 'Get in touch with our workshop team at 14 Quay Lane. Whether asking about daily flavours, arranging tub set-aside, or discussing private catering, we are glad to hear from you.',
	'pg_contact_h1' => 'General enquiries and workshop contacts',
	'pg_contact_p1' => 'For general questions, day-of flavour availability, or pickup questions, contact our front counter directly. Call us at +00 10 4820 1907 during open hours, Wednesday through Sunday from 12:00 to 21:00. You can also email hello@himurogelato.example at any time. If you are writing regarding a same-day tub reservation, remember that orders must be submitted by 15:00 so our team can pack and place your tub into the −18 °C hold shelf.',
	'pg_contact_h2' => 'Catering and wholesale partnerships',
	'pg_contact_p2' => 'We occasionally provide tubs and curated gelato service for small gatherings, local events, and independent cafes across Larkhaven. Because our kitchen churns just four litres at a time, our wholesale and catering capacity is intentionally limited. We ask for advance notice for event orders. Please send your date, guest count, and preferred flavour selections to hello@himurogelato.example, and Ines Varga will review production feasibility with our kitchen schedule.',
	'pg_contact_h3' => 'How do I reach the team when the shop is closed?',
	'pg_contact_p3' => 'On Mondays and Tuesdays, when our counter is closed for batch planning and deep cleaning, our telephone line is unmonitored. However, our email inbox at hello@himurogelato.example is monitored regularly. If you leave a message or send an email inquiry during closed days, Mei Han or Rafael Moreno will respond promptly on Wednesday morning when regular kitchen and counter service resumes.',
	'pg_contact_label' => 'Write to us',
	'pg_journal_t' => 'The Journal',
	'pg_journal_lede' => 'The Himuro Gelato journal documents our kitchen notes, batch experiments, and seasonal fruit arrivals. It is an open record of how temperature, dairy, and timing intersect at our Quay Lane workshop.',
	'pg_journal_h1' => 'Notes from the morning batch freezer',
	'pg_journal_p1' => 'Our journal serves as an ongoing log for Tomas Lind and Ines Varga as they fine-tune our daily churns. Here, we record subtle variations in milk fat content, adjustments to churn times, and notes on how ambient humidity alters base viscosity. Rather than keeping kitchen formulations hidden, we document the technical decisions behind each batch, from maintaining the eleven-minute freezer threshold to tracking how different fruit sugars interact with dairy proteins during the twelve-hour resting phase.',
	'pg_journal_h2' => 'Seasonal fruit logs and harbour harvests',
	'pg_journal_p2' => 'Written primarily by Amara Okafor, our seasonal dispatch tracks the arrival of fresh fruit at Larkhaven’s harbour markets and regional farms. Readers can follow our search for orchard figs, tart plums, and winter citrus, understanding why certain flavours appear for only a few weeks each year. These entries explain the delicate balance between natural fruit acids and sugar solids, illustrating why a simple plum ripple requires careful tasting before entering the cold slab.',
	'pg_journal_label' => 'Notes from the kitchen',
);
